## Reminders for the Cursor Agent Specifically

- Before proposing a change to memory behavior, check if it's already covered
  by a planned slice above. If yes, name the slice and align with its scope.
- Before adding a new code path that special-cases a value, ask whether the
  same outcome can come from the entity-graph mechanism. Special cases are
  the Aura failure mode and will fail `doctrine_check.sh`.
- Static strings need `.expect("...")` after `RecallReason::new`. Dynamic
  strings need to propagate the `Result`.
- `MemoryProvenance` currently allows all-`None`. Don't construct one until
  slice 3c lands (a constructor will appear that requires ≥1 source field).
